imagine that you're a red-blooded  carnivore you love burgers steak pork  chops bacon but one day out of nowhere  red meat starts to make you physically  sick to the stomach it sounds like  science fiction but it's real and it's  spreading it's spreading to people like  Amy my name is Amy pearl and I'm a  producer for WNYC she has what is called  a mammalian meat allergy I have a  tendency to not mention it at  restaurants because I feel like if you  say to a server like I'm allergic to me  they're gonna be like I'm spitting in  your food any meat that came from the  cow pig or a lamb will make a me sick  very very sick like I just had hives on  my hands and my feet and like all over  my torso was like nauseous and I felt  like I was fainting I felt like the  world was ending so I felt like I was  gonna pass out and I couldn't really  grieve thousands of Americans are  suffering like Amy but until 2009 this  sort of allergy went undiagnosed I think  I have made an appointment with my  regular physician but he immediately was  like there's no such thing as a mean  allergy has to be something else that  changed with the cancer drug is a  tuckson map in a clinical trial one for  patients developed severe allergic  reactions to the drug some even died  naturally so tuckson map was  investigated University of Virginia's  allergy Department focused on one  specific part of the drug a key  ingredient in seduction map is a  specific carbohydrate that all  non-primate mammals carry in their cell  walls and tissues galactose alpha 1 3  galactose or if you're pressed for time  alpha-gal dogs have it  cats have it and the micelles involved  in the production of say tux amount have  alpha gal  the team discovered that those who had  reactions were from only certain areas  of the u.s. the southeast the locations  of the cases aligned almost perfectly  with the range of a specific type of  tick the Lone Star tick dr. Scott  Commons is an allergist and was working  with the university at the time over 90  to 93 percent of our patients that  develop allergic reactions to red meat  and test positive by a blood test will  have a history of tick bites the thing I  googled was suddenly allergy I found an  article that said there was some man in  Florida had gone into anaphylactic shock  from eating meat after a tick bite and I  was like I had a tick bite I mean I'd  often have a tick bite I just taken a  tick off me one of the leading  researchers dr. Thomas Platts Mills went  so forests use himself in an unofficial  experiment taking a hike through a nest  of larval ticks it earned him a nice  case of red meat allergy there's still a  lot we don't know about how this meat  allergy works but here is the leading  theory ticks don't have alpha-gal  naturally but they could be carrying it  if they fed off a mammal like a deer or  a dog if a tick then bites you it trades  some of your delicious blood for its  saliva which is a cocktail of nasty  things an enzyme in that saliva tells  your body that there's a variety of  dangerous threats and your immune system  bans everything in that saliva from  entering the body including alpha-gal  which is also in every burger steak and  bacon strip so the next time you eat one  of those your body treats the  carbohydrate like an intruder and hits  the panic button this is happening in  the bodies of an estimated 5,000  Americans what's worse is that the range  of the Lone Star tick is growing their  range is spreading into the Ohio River  Valley and now up into Minnesota we also  know places where this alpha-gal red  meat allergy exists but they don't have  one-star ticks at all and this would be  southern Sweden for example there parts  of Europe  and now even South Africa so clearly  other tick species can do this as well  University of Virginia's researchers  have also linked the alpha-gal allergies  with a higher risk of heart disease this  allergy seems as though it will often go  away over time but the problem has been  that any additional picks might seem to  cause the allergy to return and these  are often patients who like to be  outside I know that my numbers have gone  down because I've been retested a couple  of times but they're still 10 20 times  what they should be dr. Cummings  continues to work towards an immediate  cure to mammalian meat allergy in the  meantime the number of cases are rising  so what we've been trying to do is work  on a vaccine related to tick saliva in  hopes that we can prevent the allergic  response from continuing or recurring  with additional tick bites if you've  been bitten by ticks recently be sure to  get tested if you haven't learned how to  explore the woods safely well if you  haven't been bitten then try to stick to  the trails if you're going into a heavy  tick infested area you may want to  consider pre treating your skin or  clothing with each or permethrin  respectively people are so freaked out  about ticks it's they're much easier to  see than you think  learn how to do a tick check after  spending time in the wilderness and if  you value a juicy steak over a walk in  nature then maybe stay out of the woods  [Music]
 

